    "title": "From Hendrix to Bowie: the trippiest music concert posters – in pictures",
    "summary": "A gallery looks back at Günther Kieser, the German artist behind some of the 20th century's most singular music posters. Drawing on sculpture, the free-form feel of jazz and psychedelic art, he designed for Jimi Hendrix, David Bowie and Diana Ross and the Supremes.",
    "source": "The Guardian",
    "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/artanddesign/gallery/2026/nov/10/gunther-kieser-concert-posters",
