    "Jazz You Can See",
    "Sound Bent Into Shape",
    "The Poster That Hums"
  ],
  "sublines": [
    "German designer Günther Kieser made concert posters inspired by sculpture, jazz improvisation and psychedelic art, now revisited in pictures.",
    "His work for Hendrix, Bowie and Diana Ross and the Supremes turned live music into singular, mind-expanding printed images.",
    "A look back at one of the 20th century's most distinctive poster artists and the free-form spirit of his designs."
